    "changelog_excerpt": "# 🚀 DMTools Release v1.7.268\n\n## 📝 What's Changed\n\nFull diff: [v1.7.267...v1.7.268](https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/compare/v1.7.267...v1.7.268)\n\n### 📦 Dependencies\n- Bump devalue from 5.9.2 to 5.9.4 in /landing (#628) (d3667694)\n- Bump dompurify from 3.4.14 to 3.4.16 in /landing (#629) (82d05ef7)\n- Bump gradle/actions/setup-gradle from 6.3.0 to 6.4.0 (#627) (593c3ada)\n\n### 🛠 Maintenance\n- Update site data for v1.7.267 (#626) (8c8e9a78)\n\n---\n\nThis release includes the **DMTools CLI** and **Agent Skill** for enterprise dark-factory orchestration across MCP tools, AI agents, and delivery workflows.\n\n## 📦 What's Included\n\n### 🖥️ DMTools CLI\n- **Command-line interface** for DMTools operations\n- **Java-based** automation and integration tools\n- **Cross-platform install scripts** for easy setup (`install`, `install.sh`, `install.bat`, `install.ps1`)\n- **Wrapper script** (`dmtools.sh`)\n\n### 🤖 DMTools Agent Skill\n- **AI assistant skill** for MCP, AI agents, and generative-ai-friendly DMTools workflows in Cursor, Claude, Codex, and other Agent Skills compatible systems\n- **Complete DMtools documentation** (67+ MCP tools, JavaScript agent development, and configuration guides)\n- **Cross-platform support** (works with all major AI coding assistants)\n\n## 🎯 Quick Start\n\n### Install DMTools CLI\n\n**macOS / Linux / Git Bash:**\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/releases/latest/download/install.sh | bash\n```\n\n**Windows (PowerShell):**\n```powershell\nirm https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/releases/latest/download/install.ps1 | iex\n```\n\n### Install DMTools Agent Skill\n\n**macOS / Linux / Git Bash:**\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/releases/download/v1.7.268/skill-install.sh | bash\n```\n\n**Windows (PowerShell):**\n```powershell\nirm https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/releases/download/v1.7.268/skill-install.ps1 | iex\n```\n\n**Focused skill install:**\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/releases/download/v1.7.268/skill-install.sh | bash -s -- --skills jira,gi..."
